<div class="text-center py-5">
  <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold"><%= ENV.fetch("APP_NAME", "Coursement Demo") %></h1>
  <p class="lead mb-3" style="color: var(--accent);">
    <%= ENV.fetch("APP_TAGLINE", "Describe a course topic. Get a complete module-by-module outline in seconds.") %>
  </p>
  <p class="text-muted mx-auto" style="max-width: 60ch;">
    <%= ENV.fetch("APP_DESCRIPTION", "") %>
  </p>
  <div class="mt-4 d-flex justify-content-center gap-3">
    <% if signed_in? %>
      <%= link_to "Go to My Courses", dashboard_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
    <% else %>
      <%= link_to "Generate your first outline", sign_up_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
      <%= link_to "Sign in", sign_in_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary btn-lg" %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row justify-content-center mt-4">
  <div class="col-lg-8">
    <p class="text-center text-muted small mb-3">Sample output</p>
    <div class="card border-draft">
      <div class="card-header d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
        <strong>Python for Data Analysis with Pandas</strong>
        <span class="badge badge-draft ms-1">Working Draft</span>
      </div>
      <div class="card-body outline-body">
        <p class="text-muted small mb-3">
          <strong>6 modules</strong> &middot; Generated just now
        </p>
        <p><strong>Target Audience:</strong> Business analysts who know Excel but have never written code<br>
        <strong>Skill Level:</strong> Beginner<br>
        <strong>Estimated Duration:</strong> 6 hours over 6 weeks</p>

        <h5>Course Overview</h5>
        <p>Learners will use Python and the Pandas library to load, clean, summarize, and visualize tabular data.
        By the end of the course they will be able to replace common Excel workflows with reproducible Python scripts.</p>

        <h6 class="mt-3">Module 1: Setting Up Your Python Environment</h6>
        <p class="text-muted small mb-1"><strong>Learning Objective:</strong> By the end of this module, learners will be able to install Python, launch a Jupyter notebook, and run their first line of code.</p>
        <ol class="mb-0">
          <li>Installing Python and Jupyter via Anaconda</li>
          <li>Navigating the Jupyter interface</li>
          <li>Variables, data types, and your first calculation</li>
        </ol>

        <h6 class="mt-3">Module 2: Loading Data with Pandas</h6>
        <p class="text-muted small mb-1"><strong>Learning Objective:</strong> By the end of this module, learners will be able to load CSV and Excel files into a DataFrame and inspect the data.</p>
        <ol class="mb-0">
          <li>What is a DataFrame?</li>
          <li>Reading CSV and Excel files</li>
          <li>Inspecting rows, columns, and data types</li>
        </ol>

        <p class="text-muted small mt-3 mb-0">+ 4 more modules&hellip;</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
